    specs_assert_against_nonexistent_product_paths_2026-08-10, 1, "2026-11-11 gate scan rewritten to ONE awk pass (xargs -0 awk, FILENAME-scoped state, single git ls-files set); previously spawned awk/sort/subshell per spec and ERRORed after >10 min; now completes in 28 min on loaded Windows host (21784 specs), selftest 5 controls pass. Offenders: 691 missing-path refs by subtree: test/03_system 316, test/system 201, test/01_unit 132, test/02_integration 33, test/feature 6, test/05_perf 3. Paths themselves NOT fixed in this lane."
    specs_assert_against_nonexistent_product_paths_2026-08-10, 2, "2026-11-11 batch (work/p2-specpaths5): scan list re-verified at a64cda1ee32 -> 494 live refs in 122 specs (PR #8326 cleared the rest). 26 refs fixed in 6 specs: vhdl_python_hdl_parity docs repointed to doc/02_requirements/hardware + doc/05_design/hardware/vhdl (deleted roadmap read dropped, its multi-DUT check moved to design doc); sugar_plugin c_backend_translate_part1 -> c_backend_translate_ops; bootstrap_pipeline qemu_runner_part1 -> part2 (token Llvm -> llvm); perf_checklists ctype bug record -> _2026-05-18.md; jupyter E2E (both trees) removed 4 always-SKIP cases whose Dockerfile + .py helpers were deleted, plus their now-unused probes. Remaining 468 refs: 379 are untracked host build-output binary probes (bin/release/<triple>/simple, src/compiler_rust/target/*/simple) in ~55 find_simple helpers -- not product paths, present on other hosts; ~45 more are build/generated outputs (bin/*_mcp_server, examples/**/*.elf, fpga_riscv generated .s, tools/*/out, tls_test_server, doc/08_tracking/baselines); the rest are intentional absence oracles (sosix future.spl/io.spl, host_winit_surface, hosted_backend_freebsd, plan-acceptance unchecked-box to_equal(false)), honest expected-FAIL to_equal(true) process gates (perf_checklists, evidence_showcase), and the specced-never-implemented c_parser (16). By subtree: test/03_system 287, test/system 181. Open: decide whether the gate should classify host build-output probes separately."
    specs_assert_against_nonexistent_product_paths_2026-08-10, 3, "2026-11-27 Windows triage & path-repair batch (release/1.0.0 7ec0a1ed579, branch work/w7-3-p2-backlog-triage-and-fixes-20261127): read-only census matching check-spec-missing-path-vacuity.shs (22440 specs, 5/5 controls PASS) found 518 (spec, path) pairs across 210 specs / 219 paths (497 unfenced, 21 fenced; test/01_unit 142, test/02_integration 35, test/03_system 330, test/05_perf 5, test/feature 6). Fixed 10 genuine moved-path refs in 6 unfenced specs (all target files verified on disk and specs executed via wa3_shared_bin simple.exe --mode=interpreter): bootstrap_api_split_contract_spec (driver/bootstrap_api -> 80.driver/bootstrap_api; 0/1 -> 1/1 PASS), native_entry_closure_gate_source_spec (driver/__init__ -> 80.driver/__init__; 3/6 -> 4/6 PASS, 2 real drift failures kept RED), stage3_streaming_route_spec (frontend/frontend -> 10.frontend/frontend, semantics/rt_criticality_validation -> 35.semantics/rt_criticality_validation, std/common/crypto/{sha512,types} -> lib/common/crypto/{sha512,types}; 1/17 -> 1/17, surfaced live source drift without weakening assertions), packed_struct_bitfield_spec (parser_decls_part2 -> _ParserDecls/enum_module_body, flat_ast_bridge_part2 -> _FlatAstBridge/module_assembly; 2/4 -> 4/4 PASS), keyof_spec (parser_primary_part2 -> _ParserPrimary/primary_expr; 1/2 -> 2/2 PASS), static_method_desugar_spec (mir_lowering_expr_part3 -> _MirLoweringExpr/method_calls_literals; 1/3 -> 2/3 PASS, 1 hir_types wording drift kept RED). After-edit census: 508 pairs across 204 specs / 209 paths (487 unfenced, 21 fenced; test/01_unit 133, test/02_integration 34, test/03_system 330, test/05_perf 5, test/feature 6), net -10 pairs / -6 specs. Status remains open for deliberate absence oracles, deleted-file controls, and host binary/artifact probes."

